pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% refused-at: parse
% The FORMULA file is malformed, so the reader rejects it before any
% rule runs. Upstream ships this as a plain incorrect instance; this
% checker additionally requires an incorrect instance to say WHERE it is
% refused, so a proof that merely stopped parsing is never mistaken for
% evidence of a checking defect.
f 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
